WEBVTT

00:00.000 --> 00:05.000
This show contains scenes that some viewers may
find disturbing.​ Viewer discretion ​is ​advised.

00:05.940 --> 00:08.490
Seriously... Why do I have to be here?

00:12.140 --> 00:13.420
Er... All right, then.

00:13.420 --> 00:16.300
Shall we get going, Goblin Slayer?

00:16.930 --> 00:17.780
Yeah.

00:17.780 --> 00:21.730
Aha, so we're heading right
into murdering those goblins.

00:21.730 --> 00:23.610
No, not exactly.

00:24.340 --> 00:25.910
We're gathering information.

00:26.350 --> 00:28.130
We're going to see the client.

00:28.130 --> 00:29.150
Huh?

02:00.010 --> 02:02.970
<b>The Red-Haired Wizard Boy</b>

02:02.010 --> 02:04.830
What? All you've got is wine?

02:04.830 --> 02:07.430
Don't you have any of
the hard stuff, brother?

02:07.430 --> 02:11.200
Only us dwarves can function after
drinking this early in the day.

02:11.200 --> 02:13.300
We've got humans here, brother.

02:14.900 --> 02:15.780
Anyway...

02:16.010 --> 02:22.320
A few days ago, this somewhat reputable
party accepted our quest...

02:22.320 --> 02:23.910
But they didn't come back.

02:23.910 --> 02:25.130
Correct.

02:26.290 --> 02:28.790
Are you the one they call Beard-cutter?

02:29.050 --> 02:31.900
Yeah. Some call me that.

02:31.900 --> 02:34.020
Goblin Slayer, eh?

02:35.180 --> 02:37.510
So what did you wanna ask about?

02:37.920 --> 02:39.220
Goblins.

02:39.220 --> 02:44.240
Well, it's not <i>just</i> goblins, 
but there are quite a few of them.

02:44.240 --> 02:47.440
I wouldn't say they're just
stealing our tools lately,

02:47.440 --> 02:50.570
but I can't have them harming
my workers in the future, either.

02:50.570 --> 02:51.920
So, goblins.

02:51.920 --> 02:57.050
Laborers are one thing, but prostitutes
and peddlers are a whole different matter.

02:57.470 --> 02:59.910
I can't pay much for 
exterminating goblins, either.

03:00.140 --> 03:02.510
That's how slaying goblins goes.

03:02.510 --> 03:07.450
Hey, Orcbolg. You haven't forgotten that
we're letting her give orders, have you?

03:07.450 --> 03:08.200
No.

03:08.830 --> 03:09.910
Really?

03:09.910 --> 03:12.000
But emergencies are different.

03:12.000 --> 03:15.110
Right. I'll be counting on
you when we're in trouble.

03:15.560 --> 03:17.000
So, um...

03:17.530 --> 03:19.830
We have a few questions for you.

03:19.830 --> 03:20.810
So, these goblins...

03:20.810 --> 03:25.720
Er, these monsters. Do you know where 
the ruins in which they're appearing are?

03:25.720 --> 03:32.140
Yeah. The fool that got his tools
stolen chased down the goblin.

03:32.140 --> 03:36.190
We can't just stand by when
some fool mishandles our tools!

03:37.270 --> 03:41.450
In that case, we'll have to get
those tools back if we find them.

03:41.660 --> 03:43.700
Yeah, thanks.

03:43.700 --> 03:49.270
Lessee. It's a bit north from
here. I'll get you a map.

03:49.270 --> 03:51.160
I think it was...

03:51.370 --> 03:52.340
A mausoleum.

03:53.500 --> 03:56.000
A place comprised of burial 
chambers and hallways.

03:56.000 --> 03:58.590
I heard it was a common design for graves.

03:58.590 --> 04:00.850
Ah, so you've heard of it.

04:00.850 --> 04:04.040
A long time ago.
I was told never to go near it.

04:04.910 --> 04:05.800
Um...

04:06.260 --> 04:10.040
Was there anything unusual about
the entrance to that grave?

04:10.040 --> 04:11.760
Perhaps some bones or a drawing?

04:11.760 --> 04:13.270
No one's mentioned anything.

04:13.270 --> 04:14.920
So no totems...

04:15.450 --> 04:19.650
Also, do you know the ranks and makeup
of the party that previously went?

04:19.650 --> 04:23.240
I'm pretty sure they were
porcelain and obsidian.

04:23.240 --> 04:26.730
They had a lizardman warrior
and a priest warrior.

04:26.730 --> 04:29.660
They also had a wizard and a priest.

04:29.680 --> 04:31.790
Also a scout or something...

04:32.040 --> 04:33.790
Were there any women in their party?

04:33.790 --> 04:39.790
Two. The priest warrior and the priest...
No, maybe she was an acolyte?

04:41.450 --> 04:42.400
Well?

04:42.400 --> 04:46.420
If they're lucky, two, but most
likely, they were all killed.

04:47.030 --> 04:51.060
We can probably assume there was
something else other than the goblins.

04:51.060 --> 04:53.350
If there weren't any totems,
there shouldn't be any shamans.

04:53.830 --> 04:56.910
Hobgoblins will be easy,
but we need to watch out for traps.

04:56.910 --> 04:59.060
I'd guess there are about
thirty or so of them.

04:59.060 --> 05:01.900
But I'm sure their numbers
must have gone down a little.

05:02.290 --> 05:05.770
I highly doubt the party of
five couldn't kill even one.

05:06.990 --> 05:08.920
You're not gonna do anything?

05:08.920 --> 05:10.810
You gotta have the right
people in the right places.

05:10.810 --> 05:13.440
My job is to be a ranger and scout.

05:13.440 --> 05:14.790
They can do the rest.

05:15.030 --> 05:16.860
That's right, lad.

05:16.860 --> 05:20.250
I guess even long-ears can say something
sensible every once in a while.

05:20.250 --> 05:23.370
Pacing is important for spell casters.

05:23.370 --> 05:26.540
I always only say sensible things.

05:26.540 --> 05:27.740
Is that so?

05:27.740 --> 05:28.810
It sure is!

05:29.630 --> 05:33.000
Anyway, the point is,
everyone has a job to do.

05:33.000 --> 05:36.230
Job? You mean other than being,
like, a warrior or wizard?

05:36.600 --> 05:39.440
Um, could you all gather around?

05:39.440 --> 05:40.650
What is it?

05:42.990 --> 05:46.610
All we have to do is kill some 
goblins. What else matters?

05:50.040 --> 05:51.650
I see.

05:51.650 --> 05:54.560
Yeah, I can definitely imagine
kids wanting to play in there.

05:54.560 --> 05:57.160
That's why I was told to stay away.

05:57.160 --> 05:59.750
So, did you ever go near one?

05:59.990 --> 06:04.620
No. But I heard they consist
of burial chambers and hallways.

06:05.190 --> 06:07.520
That's what my older sister told me.

06:08.460 --> 06:11.260
Regardless, that's in the past.

06:11.260 --> 06:13.590
Let's hurry up and go in already.

06:13.590 --> 06:15.780
There are other adventurers
captured in there, right?

06:18.390 --> 06:20.400
We need to hurry up and save them.

06:24.240 --> 06:29.320
"Haste makes waste." This saying
has been around for centuries.

06:29.320 --> 06:30.280
Right.

06:32.610 --> 06:33.950
Everyone.

06:33.950 --> 06:35.820
Are you ready?

06:36.910 --> 06:40.820
What shall our formation be, lady leader?

06:40.820 --> 06:45.460
Oh, stop that. You're really 
enjoying this, aren't you?

06:46.020 --> 06:47.230
As for our formation...

06:47.230 --> 06:50.800
We have a party of six this time,
so let's have three rows of two.

06:50.800 --> 06:54.260
That'll make it easier to 
switch rows if we need to.

06:54.260 --> 06:57.810
Got it. I guess we'll have to
do that if our leader says so.

06:57.810 --> 06:59.570
Please, stop already.

06:59.570 --> 07:01.520
Oh, and...

07:01.930 --> 07:03.710
Wh-What?

07:04.690 --> 07:06.700
We need to get rid of our scent.

07:08.690 --> 07:09.890
Huh?

07:20.770 --> 07:23.040
Goblins. Five of them.

07:29.430 --> 07:30.420
That's one.

07:32.570 --> 07:33.260
That's two!

07:38.820 --> 07:40.060
Damn it!

07:40.060 --> 07:42.390
Carbunculus... Crescunt...

07:42.390 --> 07:43.950
Don't use your spells yet!

07:44.370 --> 07:45.190
The door!

07:45.190 --> 07:46.570
Got it!

07:50.870 --> 07:53.780
Looks like we're all right for now.

07:53.780 --> 07:58.010
Well, I do hope I get to do something.

07:58.010 --> 07:59.290
Still too many enemies.

07:59.500 --> 08:03.740
Well, then... I guess it 
wouldn't do to hesitate.

08:10.350 --> 08:12.720
Should we really be moving this slowly?

08:13.150 --> 08:16.050
It's very dangerous, so we have
to take it one room at a time.

08:16.050 --> 08:17.390
Yeah, but...

08:17.710 --> 08:20.070
The captured people are in danger.

08:23.080 --> 08:24.980
How are the other rooms?

08:24.980 --> 08:27.530
They're unlocked, and no enemies around.

08:27.530 --> 08:29.880
But look over there.

08:33.020 --> 08:34.030
A trap?

08:34.030 --> 08:35.410
Probably.

08:35.410 --> 08:36.530
That's a pain.

08:36.530 --> 08:41.620
Come to think of it, they said that
the goblins stole their tools.

08:43.450 --> 08:46.540
Well, I don't even want to 
think about what those goblins

08:46.540 --> 08:48.460
plan to do with those carpentry tools.

08:49.180 --> 08:54.630
There's not much of a load on it, so I
can't imagine it's a complicated trap.

08:54.630 --> 08:57.920
We do also have the option
of going down another path.

08:57.920 --> 09:01.100
It appears that the other goblins
haven't noticed we're here.

09:06.060 --> 09:08.230
Damn it! This is taking forever!

09:08.590 --> 09:10.650
The goblins live here, don't they?!

09:11.020 --> 09:13.200
Then they wouldn't have any traps here!

09:13.200 --> 09:13.750
Move!

09:13.750 --> 09:14.740
Hey, wait a minute!

09:14.740 --> 09:15.950
What do you think you're—

09:15.950 --> 09:17.610
I'm opening this.

09:17.610 --> 09:19.580
<i>Huh? W-Wai—</i>

09:19.580 --> 09:23.080
<i>I have to stop him! What do I say?
How do I convince him?</i>

09:23.430 --> 09:25.080
<i>Goblin Slayer!</i>

09:25.080 --> 09:28.210
<i>What should I do? What should I do?
What should I do? What should I do?</i>

09:34.190 --> 09:37.990
Wh-Wh-Wh-Wh-Wh-Wh-Wh-What the...

09:39.320 --> 09:41.050
The goblins are messing around.

09:41.050 --> 09:42.690
This is bad.

09:43.380 --> 09:45.490
His scream definitely acted as an alarm.

09:45.490 --> 09:46.810
That's how it's set up.

09:47.370 --> 09:48.940
They'll be here any minute.

09:51.860 --> 09:53.170
A scream?

09:53.560 --> 09:54.150
This way!

09:55.140 --> 09:56.980
Don't take off on your own!

10:02.840 --> 10:03.740
Is this it?

10:06.100 --> 10:08.370
Are you here?! I'm here to save—

10:20.960 --> 10:25.560
C-Carbunculus... C-Crescunt... Iacta!

10:33.370 --> 10:34.860
Hey, are you okay?!

10:36.250 --> 10:38.250
I'll get you out of here right away!

11:33.130 --> 11:35.000
Stay back! It's a trap!

11:42.150 --> 11:43.610
Count, twenty.

11:51.600 --> 11:53.810
Sixteen left. Are you alive?

11:54.560 --> 11:55.900
Y-Yeah.

11:55.900 --> 11:56.490
Not you.

11:56.490 --> 11:59.410
He is referring to the girl over there.

11:59.980 --> 12:00.910
She is!

12:02.280 --> 12:04.490
She's still alive! Of course she is!

12:04.490 --> 12:05.760
I see.

12:05.760 --> 12:08.130
I wanted to save her as quickly as I could...

12:08.130 --> 12:10.310
We also have women on our team.

12:11.620 --> 12:12.660
Two of them.

12:12.660 --> 12:13.960
For crying out loud...

12:13.960 --> 12:16.920
This is why I hate goblins.

12:20.090 --> 12:21.140
B-But...

12:21.140 --> 12:24.800
No time for yappin'!
Just take the whole chair with us!

12:36.560 --> 12:37.980
Hold that side!

12:37.980 --> 12:38.270
Okay.

12:38.270 --> 12:41.760
Still more coming from the back.
What do you want to do?

12:42.550 --> 12:44.890
U-Um... Uh...

12:44.890 --> 12:46.250
Sir Goblin Slayer.

12:46.650 --> 12:48.530
Yeah. You ready?

12:52.670 --> 12:53.750
Holy Light.

12:53.750 --> 12:54.210
Right!

12:54.210 --> 12:56.670
Well cut straight through.
I'll leave the vanguard to you.

12:56.670 --> 12:57.500
Understood!

12:57.780 --> 13:00.220
I'll take care of that screaming giant.

13:00.670 --> 13:04.270
By yourself?! That's impossible!
You're dealing with a troll!

13:04.270 --> 13:05.510
You dumb boy.

13:05.510 --> 13:09.220
This is exactly the kind of 
moment when Orcbolg shines!

13:09.220 --> 13:11.500
O merciful Earth Mother, please bless us,

13:11.820 --> 13:16.140
the wanderers in the
darkness, with holy light!

13:16.140 --> 13:17.640
Holy Light!

13:23.220 --> 13:24.240
Let's go!

13:33.140 --> 13:34.000
A troll?

13:35.470 --> 13:37.170
You're not a goblin.

13:48.730 --> 13:49.630
Bye.

13:58.450 --> 14:00.250
That should've taken care of half of them.

14:00.740 --> 14:01.800
In which case...

14:04.940 --> 14:06.110
That's fifteen.

14:07.320 --> 14:09.070
Hey, Orcbolg!

14:09.290 --> 14:12.230
I heard some kind of booming
noise from behind us.

14:12.230 --> 14:15.380
It was an emergency. 
How's it looking in front?

14:15.380 --> 14:16.540
Same as always!

14:17.630 --> 14:20.000
Hi-yah! Let's go all-out!

14:20.000 --> 14:21.460
So, do you have a plan?

14:21.460 --> 14:24.410
I do. I always do.

14:29.100 --> 14:30.840
We're trapped, damn it!

14:33.190 --> 14:36.340
Now, now, we don't know that for sure.

14:37.640 --> 14:41.170
U-Um... Where are Goblin
Slayer and High Elf Archer?

14:41.170 --> 14:43.430
They'll catch up soon enough.

14:44.330 --> 14:45.410
Here.

14:47.850 --> 14:49.110
Thank you.

14:53.570 --> 14:55.910
We need to treat her wounds at once.

14:55.910 --> 14:57.790
Nah, you take a breather.

14:58.800 --> 15:01.590
She's not so injured that
she could die at any moment.

15:01.590 --> 15:03.250
You good, lad?

15:03.250 --> 15:04.490
I'm fine.

15:04.490 --> 15:05.560
I see.

15:11.530 --> 15:15.890
I bet when you're in trouble, you're shaking
in your boots and just calling for God.

15:17.720 --> 15:19.410
S-So, hey... I'm s—

15:19.410 --> 15:20.530
They're here!

15:21.310 --> 15:24.520
Damn it, Orcbolg! That thing's still alive!

15:24.810 --> 15:26.720
I guess it's tougher than I thought.

15:31.080 --> 15:33.330
I'm so done with this!
What the heck is that thing?!

15:33.330 --> 15:36.120
I wanted to fight something
that looks cooler!

15:36.120 --> 15:37.790
What're we gonna do, Beard-cutter?

15:38.020 --> 15:39.000
I need water.

15:39.000 --> 15:40.380
Can you make some with a spell?

15:40.380 --> 15:43.100
There's no point in memorizing
spells like that.

15:42.190 --> 15:43.500
I've got some rain!

15:43.750 --> 15:46.020
Though it'll be a bit
weak since we're inside.

15:46.020 --> 15:47.010
That's fine.

15:47.500 --> 15:49.500
Also, we need Holy Light one more time.

15:50.490 --> 15:51.470
Can you do it?

15:53.600 --> 15:55.130
I-I can!

15:55.130 --> 15:55.640
Good.

15:59.230 --> 16:01.330
O merciful Earth Mother, please bless us,

16:01.330 --> 16:05.530
the wanderers in the
darkness, with holy light!

16:06.520 --> 16:08.250
Holy Light!

16:10.150 --> 16:11.290
I need that water.

16:11.290 --> 16:12.070
You got it!

16:12.300 --> 16:14.700
Go forth, Kelpie. Go boldly!

16:14.700 --> 16:17.610
From earth to river and sea to sky!

16:17.610 --> 16:19.610
Call Rain!

16:29.450 --> 16:31.760
Next... is this.

16:39.110 --> 16:41.740
Wh-What the? The troll's body is...

16:48.420 --> 16:50.040
It's simple, but not bad.

16:51.010 --> 16:52.190
What just happened?

16:52.510 --> 16:55.870
If you quickly cool down 
heated stone, it can break.

16:56.220 --> 16:58.880
That secret formula is sucking up
the water and that thing's heat,

16:58.880 --> 17:00.310
and freezing it instantly.

17:00.640 --> 17:02.360
Apparently that's how it works.

17:03.980 --> 17:05.910
Where the heck did you learn that?

17:05.910 --> 17:07.150
Water Town.

17:07.150 --> 17:09.350
Oh! The ice treats?

17:10.780 --> 17:13.550
It seems to be suffering
from wounds that won't heal.

17:13.550 --> 17:15.880
How unfortunate for it.

17:16.330 --> 17:18.850
Once we finish off that giant, 
inexplicable thing...

17:20.810 --> 17:23.310
We're going to slay all the goblins.

17:49.720 --> 17:52.210
<i>I know this happened partially
because I was careless.</i>

17:52.650 --> 17:55.630
<i>I'm still green,
and this is my responsibility.</i>

17:55.970 --> 17:56.840
<i>But...</i>

17:57.860 --> 18:00.160
<i>This guy who seemed so blasé
about fighting the troll,</i>

18:00.820 --> 18:04.800
<i>but so delighted about killing the goblins...</i>

18:05.680 --> 18:06.640
<i>I...</i>

18:07.700 --> 18:09.810
<i>This is the only guy...</i>

18:11.070 --> 18:12.530
<i>that I refuse to acknowledge!</i>

18:15.470 --> 18:17.450
Well, all right, then.

18:17.450 --> 18:22.410
To the fact that we survived! To that
monster's head! To that acolyte's future!

18:22.410 --> 18:24.610
Cheers!

18:22.410 --> 18:24.610
Cheers!

18:26.480 --> 18:28.660
Oh, pardon me, waitress!

18:28.660 --> 18:32.040
Could you bring me some cheese-covered
sausages right away?

18:32.040 --> 18:35.510
Sure, you've got it, Mr. Lizardman!
Your usual!

18:35.510 --> 18:37.230
Oh, come on, Orcbolg!

18:37.230 --> 18:40.280
Why do you always go silent
at times like these?

18:40.280 --> 18:41.040
Do I?

18:41.040 --> 18:42.490
You do.

18:42.490 --> 18:44.230
Go on. You drink, too.

18:44.230 --> 18:47.680
I'm, uh... Today isn't really...

18:47.680 --> 18:49.670
Oh, come on!

18:49.670 --> 18:52.470
You're alive! That's all that matters!

18:52.470 --> 18:56.070
No one's gonna be perfect at
giving orders right off the bat!

18:56.070 --> 18:59.450
Also, what's going on with you over there?

19:01.240 --> 19:04.180
Now, cheer up.

19:04.180 --> 19:08.420
You made it back from your first adventure
alive. That is reason to celebrate.

19:08.420 --> 19:10.080
That's right, lad!

19:10.940 --> 19:15.370
Not many get to face a troll
on their first adventure!

19:16.220 --> 19:17.840
If that troll hadn't shown up...

19:18.110 --> 19:20.370
Even I could've handled those goblins...

19:21.320 --> 19:25.070
I also wish that I had done better...

19:25.070 --> 19:27.270
Such admirable spirit!

19:27.270 --> 19:29.930
Nothing can be done until
you put your mind to it!

19:29.930 --> 19:32.980
They say that progress only
happens one step at a time.

19:33.780 --> 19:36.040
My ancestor, the fearsome dragon,

19:36.040 --> 19:40.860
evolved from a four-legged 
creature in the swamplands.

19:40.860 --> 19:42.570
Uh-huh...

19:42.930 --> 19:44.780
Hey, by the way...

19:44.780 --> 19:47.580
What happened to that acolyte?

19:47.580 --> 19:50.610
Oh, right. Her wounds 
were treated, and she said

19:50.610 --> 19:53.000
she'll think about what to 
do next once she recovers.

19:53.000 --> 19:54.960
I see. Well, that's good.

19:54.960 --> 19:56.980
That might be a weird thing to say,

19:56.980 --> 19:58.800
but you can always move on
as long as you're alive.

19:59.070 --> 20:01.260
Being alive isn't going to solve everything.

20:02.220 --> 20:06.350
She lost to goblins. People are 
obviously going to mock her.

20:06.350 --> 20:10.100
Wh-What's your problem? That's not—

20:10.350 --> 20:12.560
That's what happened to my older sister!

20:13.270 --> 20:16.730
They kept saying that she lost to goblins!
That she was killed by goblins!

20:17.090 --> 20:19.530
Older sister? You have an older sister?

20:19.530 --> 20:20.900
Yeah, I did!

20:21.220 --> 20:24.110
If she hadn't been stabbed by 
goblins with a poisoned dagger,

20:24.110 --> 20:25.370
she'd still be here right now!

20:25.690 --> 20:26.520
What?

20:34.020 --> 20:36.130
My sister was amazing!

20:36.130 --> 20:38.680
She would've beaten them 
if they hadn't used poison!

20:41.950 --> 20:47.350
And yet... All those guys at the academy...
kept running their mouths...

20:47.350 --> 20:48.940
They can...

20:48.940 --> 20:51.550
They can all just die...

20:52.350 --> 20:53.340
I see.

20:56.180 --> 20:57.380
I'm heading back.

20:58.290 --> 21:03.030
Someone get him a room somewhere.
It doesn't matter where.

21:03.030 --> 21:05.100
Yup, you got it.

21:06.730 --> 21:08.400
Goblin Slayer.

21:09.800 --> 21:11.910
Get some rest.

21:13.860 --> 21:17.080
Hey, Orcbolg! What are we doing tomorrow?

21:17.080 --> 21:18.110
I don't know.

21:20.040 --> 21:24.010
